      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-27T16:39:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t this going to cause a SHA3 to happen for every tiny DAWN_SERIALIZABLE thing? IMHO we should do the checks when storing / retrieving at the dawn::platform level.",
      "revId": "dd1c558a13dfd58fb5039abd388659a49995e5f2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "036b2277_b1cbf8d8",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Serializable.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-27T18:59:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 for doing this at the platform level. In Dawn this could probably be in the `BlobCache` class: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/BlobCache.h;drc\u003de65323be17a0ba06198d18b0a8bf5ae594e10348;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0;l\u003d48",
      "parentUuid": "581c885e_20f63e9a",
      "revId": "dd1c558a13dfd58fb5039abd388659a49995e5f2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "836d1c9f_4f781651",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Serializable.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-28T01:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I get it right `ToBlob`/`FromBlob` are not recursive, they call `StreamIn`/`StreamOut` inside (which are recursive on every member).\n\nWe can do the validation in `BlobCache::LoadInternal` and `StoreInternal`, but that would introduce a full memory copy within `StoreInternal` because `Blob` just hold a pointer to raw memory and platform cache functions also expect a pointer to raw memory, but adding hash will change the byte size and must allocate a new buffer for whole hash+payload.",
      "parentUuid": "036b2277_b1cbf8d8",
      "revId": "dd1c558a13dfd58fb5039abd388659a49995e5f2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "250dcdec_3e29f458",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Serializable.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-28T04:16:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we would probably want to add an additional argument to those functions that explicitly pass the hash. Then we could do a transition to use those functions instead of the existing ones.",
      "parentUuid": "836d1c9f_4f781651",
      "revId": "dd1c558a13dfd58fb5039abd388659a49995e5f2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "834e81d4_ca607ae1",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Serializable.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-28T05:38:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That might change a lot of code as I thought the cache functions are provided by platform i.e. chromium?\n\nI can try the `LoadInternal`/`StoreInternal` method.",
      "parentUuid": "250dcdec_3e29f458",
      "revId": "dd1c558a13dfd58fb5039abd388659a49995e5f2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54784b03_e7e8bfa4",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Serializable.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-01T22:56:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oof... I see what you mean about needing the full copy... It might not be ideal, but maybe the right way is to do the bigger change incrementally? i.e. we introduce new callback functions in this CL while still supporting the other path, then migrate chromium to use the callback functions (that now take an additional integrity hash key argument).\n\nI feel like the copy will likely be a decent perf regression unfortunately. Another (probably hacky) solution, is we could store the integrity hash separately? Maybe we would set it up so that the the existing (cache key)-\u003e(integrity hash), then (optional? cache key + integrity hash)-\u003e(actual blob), or something like that? That would mean invoking the callback functions twice for both load and store though. Honestly though, it feels like these ideas would just be like tech-debt workarounds, so IMO we should just do it the clean way.",
      "parentUuid": "834e81d4_ca607ae1",
      "revId": "dd1c558a13dfd58fb5039abd388659a49995e5f2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04d41fd2_ee86586a",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Serializable.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-02T03:35:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if it is worthy to change the Chromium cache implementation to explicitly handle the separated hash, as it would change a lot of code (at least we have to change the `DawnCachingInterface`), considering this hash validation might be temporary and the Chromium blob cache system might be going to get refactored.\n\n@cwallez@chromium.org, what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "54784b03_e7e8bfa4",
      "revId": "dd1c558a13dfd58fb5039abd388659a49995e5f2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
